From 067548029740ef2a6aebfdfb24f5c580f11fc138 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 06:25:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/10] perf(client): stop resending sensor power requests
 every frame

While a vehicle head was over an unpowered redstone sensor, the client sent
PacketTurnOnBlockEntity every frame until the powered state made the round
trip. The server's power() only raises the sensor to level 2 and schedules
the decay tick once from level 0, so these repeats were no-ops. Track the last
request per sensor position and world, and send again only when the observed
power level differs or 250 ms have passed without a change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TD7PJ5R7t7hM3ymeeqXP4H
